You take the Magic Mirror!  Congratulations!	你拿到了魔鏡！恭喜你！
Dragon's Tongue is considered a delicacy in some parts of the world, but not in Daventry!	龍舌在世界某些地方被視為珍饈，但在戴凡確王國可不是！
The dragon took it with him.	巨龍把它一起帶走了。
This boulder is far too heavy to move.	這塊巨石太重了，搬不動。
As you slowly and silently return to visibility, the dragon fails to notice you.	你緩緩無聲地現出身形，巨龍卻沒有注意到你。
There is no one here to receive your offering.	這裡沒有人可以接受你的獻禮。
The dead dragon does not need anything you have to offer.	死去的巨龍不需要你所能奉上的任何東西。
The dragon, unaware that you've stolen his great treasure, is not interested in anything you have to offer.	巨龍還不知道你已偷走牠的寶物，對你所能奉上的東西毫無興趣。
The dragon isn't interested in any of your possessions.  It's already got one of the most valuable treasures in Daventry.	巨龍對你身上的任何東西都沒興趣，牠已經擁有戴凡確王國最珍貴的寶物之一。
Parts of the cave are made impassable by huge, jagged stalagmites.	洞穴裡有些地方被巨大嶙峋的石筍擋住，無法通行。
The craggy limestone stalactites hang menacingly from the roof of the cavern.	嶙峋的石灰岩鐘乳石從洞頂懸垂而下，看來十分嚇人。
Smoking is bad for your health.  That's why there are not many dragons around.	抽菸有害健康。這就是為什麼巨龍已經不多見了。
The dragon's head is angular, like a pterodactyl's.  Large webbed gill flaps protrude from either side of his face, just underneath his horns.  Smoke curls lazily from his nostrils.	巨龍的頭部稜角分明，像翼手龍一樣。臉頰兩側、犄角下方各突出一片巨大的蹼狀鰓瓣，鼻孔裡懶洋洋地冒出裊裊青煙。
Green and scaly, the dragon's body is massive and muscular.  A row of serrated armor stretches from the tip of his tail to the base of his neck; his leathery wings are folded tight against his sides, and his webbed claws look sharp and deadly.	巨龍全身覆滿綠色鱗片，體型龐大、肌肉結實。一排鋸齒狀的甲殼從尾尖延伸到頸根；牠那對皮革般的翅膀緊緊收攏在身側，蹼狀的爪子看來銳利致命。
You should get closer to the mirror.	你應該靠近魔鏡一點。
The mirror shimmers with its own magical light.	魔鏡散發著自身的魔法光芒，微微閃爍。
The dragon's long, powerful neck is a slinky mass of sinew and scales. The underside of his throat is pale, fleshy and unprotected by scales.	巨龍那條修長強壯的脖子，是一團柔韌的肌腱與鱗片。牠喉嚨下方的皮膚蒼白柔軟，沒有鱗片保護。
The dragon lies motionless on the rocky floor of the cavern.	巨龍一動也不動地躺在洞穴的岩石地面上。
The ferocious fire-breathing dragon may look asleep, but don't be fooled....he's smarter than he looks.	這隻兇猛的噴火巨龍看起來像是睡著了，但別被騙了……牠比看起來聰明得多。
There is a vicious fire-breathing dragon here!	這裡有一隻兇猛的噴火巨龍！
Ordinarily, music hath charms to soothe a savage beast but this beast is a little too ferocious to appreciate fiddle music.	通常音樂能撫慰凶猛的野獸，但這頭野獸太過兇殘，欣賞不了小提琴的樂聲。
This dragon had only one life, and you have already taken it.	這隻巨龍只有一條命，而你已經取走了。
You don't have anything sharp enough to pierce the dragon's scaly hide!	你身上沒有夠鋒利的東西，能刺穿巨龍的鱗皮！
Wait and see what the dragon is doing first.	先等等，看看巨龍在做什麼。
You don't have everything you need to attempt such a feat.	你身上還缺少嘗試這項壯舉所需的東西。
The dragon's already dead. Shooting him would be a waste of pebbles.	巨龍已經死了，朝牠射擊只是浪費鵝卵石。
The pebbles are too blunt to deliver a fatal blow to the dragon, maybe a different approach would be better.	鵝卵石太鈍了，沒辦法對巨龍造成致命一擊，或許該換個方法。
The dragon is dead.  He can no longer hear you.	巨龍已經死了，聽不見你說話了。
Think again.  When this dragon talks, things have a tendency to catch fire.	再想想吧。這隻巨龍一開口說話，東西可是會著火的。
The mere thought of retrieving the dagger repulses you.	光是想到要去撿回那把短刀，就讓你感到反胃。
How?	怎麼做？
The dragon is dead. He has ceased to be. Bereft of life, he rests in peace. Best to get on with the game and forget this sad creature.	巨龍死了。牠已經不在了。失去了生命，安息長眠。還是繼續玩下去，忘了這隻可悲的生物吧。
Be careful.  Dragons are very dangerous.	小心點，巨龍非常危險。
The Fairy Godmother's protective spell has saved you from a fiery fate.	教母的守護魔法救了你，讓你逃過一場火劫。
The dagger flies through the air and is lost in the cave's darkness.	短刀飛過半空，消失在洞穴的黑暗之中。
With unerring aim, the dagger streaks through the air and pierces the soft, unprotected skin under the dragon's throat.  The dragon convulses for a moment, and then crashes, lifeless, to the hard cavern floor.	短刀精準無比地劃過空中，刺入巨龍喉嚨下方柔軟無鱗的皮膚。巨龍抽搐了片刻，隨即癱軟倒地，重重摔在堅硬的洞穴地面上，沒了氣息。
Good shot!  The water hits the dragon square in the face, dousing the dragon's fire.	好一擊！水正中巨龍的臉，澆熄了牠的火焰。
Unable to defend itself with anything more than harmless clouds of steam, the dragon rolls aside the granite boulder and slinks off in shame, leaving the mirror behind.	巨龍除了噴出無害的蒸汽，再也無力自保，只好推開那塊花崗岩巨石，羞愧地溜走，留下了魔鏡。
Unable to defend itself with anything more than harmless clouds of steam, the dragon rolls aside the granite boulder and slinks off in shame.	巨龍除了噴出無害的蒸汽，再也無力自保，只好推開那塊花崗岩巨石，羞愧地溜走了。
You can't do that while you are invisible.	你隱形的時候沒辦法這麼做。
As your nose fills with the aroma of fresh well water, your lungs give out. Don't smell the water!	井水清新的氣味灌滿你的鼻腔，你的肺卻撐不住了。別去聞水的味道！
It's too late to dive.  At this point, all you can do is drown.	已經來不及潛水了，事到如今你只能溺水。
You are already doing that!	你已經在這麼做了！
You need to be swimming first.	你得先開始游泳。
Too late!  You have already stopped swimming and started drowning.	太遲了！你已經停止游泳，開始溺水了。
Just walk over to the water.	走到水邊就行了。
You're already in the water.	你已經在水裡了。
You've swum too long already!  Your endurance has run out.	你游得太久了！體力已經耗盡。
You can't do that from under water!	你在水底下沒辦法這麼做！
There's no reason to climb anything here.	這裡沒有什麼好爬的。
This isn't the chest you're looking for.	這不是你要找的箱子。
All you have to do is walk right into the water.	你只需要直接走進水裡就行了。
What would you like to get into?	你想要進去什麼裡面？
You take a deep drink of the cold well water.	你大口暢飲冰涼的井水。
The hinges are rusted, but still very strong.	鉸鏈雖然鏽蝕，卻依然十分堅固。
This dark pool of water leads to the bottom of the ancient well near King Edward's castle.	這片幽暗的水潭，通往愛德華國王城堡附近那口古井的井底。
You are too far away to see clearly.	你離得太遠，看不清楚。
Too late!  Your vision grows blurred as you go down for the third time.	太遲了！你第三次沉下水面，視線逐漸模糊。
You can see the surface of the water just above you.	你看見水面就在你的正上方。
You can just see the opening of the well far above you.	你隱約看見井口在你頭頂遙遠的上方。
You see the low ceiling of the cave just above you.	你看見洞穴低矮的頂部，就在你頭頂上方。
You can see the bottom of the well below you.	你看見井底就在你的下方。
You are at the bottom of the well.  Through the plants you spy what seems to be a hole in the side of the well.	你正位於井底。透過水草，你瞥見井壁側面似乎有個洞。
The cave is dark and very damp.	這座洞穴幽暗又十分潮濕。
This looks like typical well water.	這看起來就是普通的井水。
The chest is buried deep in the sand and is too heavy to carry.	箱子深埋在沙裡，重得搬不動。
The lid's hinges are rusted shut.	蓋子的鉸鏈已經鏽死了。
The half-buried chest looks as if it has been here for a very long time.	這只半埋在沙中的箱子，看起來已經在這裡放了很長一段時間。
It looks like this chest has been buried here for a very long time.	這只箱子看起來已經埋在這裡很長一段時間了。
As you get into the water, the magic ring slips from your finger and vanishes.	你進入水中時，魔戒從你的手指上滑落，消失無蹤。
This looks like a typical weed.	這看起來是一株普通的水草。
More curious still, the courtyard is deserted; this area is usually filled with the Ladies and Lords of the castle.	更奇怪的是，庭院裡空無一人；這裡平常總是擠滿城堡裡的貴族仕女與紳士。
This is highly unusual.  You begin to feel deeply disturbed, as if all is not right within the castle.	這實在不尋常。你開始感到一陣不安，彷彿城堡裡出了什麼問題。
You can faintly hear a commotion in the King's Chamber to the west.	你隱約聽見西邊國王寢宮傳來一陣騷動。
DOCTOR:  "There's nothing to be done."	御醫：「已經無能為力了。」
DOCTOR:  "Our King's melancholy is too much for his heart to bear.  Perhaps if Sir Graham had returned with the three lost treasures of Daventry ..."	御醫：「國王陛下的憂鬱，他的心臟已經承受不住了。若是格拉漢爵士能帶回戴凡確王國失落的三件寶物就好了……」
SIR GRAHAM:  "Your Highness, I am at your service."	格拉漢爵士：「陛下，臣聽候差遣。」
KING:  "Did ... did you succeed in your quest?"	國王：「你……你的任務成功了嗎？」
SIR GRAHAM:  "I did, Your Majesty."	格拉漢爵士：「成功了，陛下。」
SIR GRAHAM:  "Here, as you commanded ..."	格拉漢爵士：「這是遵照您的命令……」
SIR GRAHAM:  "...the magic mirror."	格拉漢爵士：「……魔鏡。」
SIR GRAHAM:  "...the magic shield."	格拉漢爵士：「……靈盾。」
SIR GRAHAM:  "...and the magic chest."	格拉漢爵士：「……還有金盒子。」
KING:  "I...I am afraid it is a little too late for me.  But you have done superbly, my Knight.  As I promised, the kingdom is yours."	國王：「我……恐怕，對我來說已經太遲了。但你的表現無比出色，我的騎士。如我所承諾的，這個王國從此屬於你。」
KING:  "I know you will serve her well."	國王：「我知道你會好好守護她。」
DOCTOR:  "The King is dead."	御醫：「國王駕崩了。」
DOCTOR:  "Long live the King!"	御醫：「吾王萬歲！」
CROWD:  "Long live the King!"	群眾：「吾王萬歲！」
And thus ended Sir Graham's great quest for the lost treasures of Daventry.  Despite the loss of their beloved King Edward, the people of Daventry grew happy and prosperous and flourished for years to come.	格拉漢爵士尋找戴凡確王國失落寶物的偉大冒險，就此告一段落。儘管痛失敬愛的愛德華國王，戴凡確的百姓依然日漸富足安樂，往後多年欣欣向榮。
And whenever King Graham looked into his magic mirror, he saw visions of adventures yet to come...for him, for his children, and for Daventry, the land he loved so much.	每當格拉漢國王凝視他的魔鏡，總能看見未來冒險的景象……那是屬於他、屬於他的子女，也屬於他深愛的戴凡確王國的冒險。
The End.	劇終。
"GASP!"	「倒抽一口氣！」
"It's Sir Graham!"	「是格拉漢爵士！」
"He's returned!"	「他回來了！」
"Did he find the treasures?"	「他找到寶物了嗎？」
"Shhhhhh!"	「噓——！」
"Listen!"	「聽！」
The giant is lying dead on the ground; beside him is a sturdy chest.	巨人倒臥在地上死去，身旁擺著一只堅固的金盒子。
The giant is asleep, with a chest lying next to him.	巨人正睡著，身旁擺著一只金盒子。
The enormous giant has been carrying that heavy chest for longer than he can remember.	這個巨大的巨人揹著那只沉重的金盒子，久到他自己都不記得多久了。
The giant is lying dead on the ground, slain by a pebble to the forehead.	巨人倒臥在地上死去，額頭中了一顆鵝卵石而喪命。
The huge giant has fallen asleep and is now snoring loudly.	這個巨大的巨人睡著了，正打著響亮的呼嚕。
The giant is enormous!  He does look rather stupid, though.	這個巨人真是龐大！不過看起來也挺蠢的。
A dead giant does not have a lot to say.	死去的巨人沒什麼好說的。
It is not a good idea to wake a sleeping giant.	叫醒沉睡的巨人可不是個好主意。
The giant is in no mood for talking.	巨人沒心情說話。
No matter how much noise you make, you can't wake the dead!	不管你製造多大的聲響，都叫不醒死人！
This giant is already awake...and he's in a bad mood!	這個巨人已經醒了……而且心情很差！
Tickling a dead giant?  The thin air up here must be affecting your mind.	搔死去的巨人癢？這裡稀薄的空氣，一定影響了你的腦子。
The giant isn't ticklish.  And it's a good thing for you that he isn't!	這個巨人不怕癢，而這對你來說可是件好事！
Getting that close to the giant would be dangerous. Besides, you couldn't reach his weak spot.	靠巨人那麼近太危險了。再說，你也碰不到他的弱點。
You don't anything sharp enough to even try that.	你身上沒有夠鋒利的東西，連試都沒辦法試。
You'll need something to help you kill the giant -- if that's how you want to defeat him!	如果你想用這種方式打倒巨人，就需要一些工具來幫你！
You need some kind of small rock to use the sling.	你需要某種小石頭才能使用投石器。
With the giant going to sleep, it would be unnecessary and cruel to kill him.	巨人已經睡著了，殺他既沒必要又太殘忍。
With what?	用什麼？
If you're trying to knock out the giant, don't bother.  He's already knocked out from chasing you.	如果你想打昏巨人，別費心了，他追你追到已經自己昏過去了。
Now that he's dead, the giant couldn't care less what you want to give him.	巨人已經死了，你想給他什麼，他根本不在乎。
The giant does not need anything.  All he wants from you is to grind your bones to dust.	巨人什麼都不需要，他對你唯一的念頭，就是把你的骨頭磨成粉。
The giant, with his chest, has all the treasure he needs; all he wants from you is to grind your bones to dust.	巨人有了他的金盒子，該有的寶物都有了；他對你唯一的念頭，就是把你的骨頭磨成粉。
You have no reason to do that.	你沒有理由這麼做。
You see nothing of interest on the ground.	地上沒看到什麼有趣的東西。
There is a chest near the sleeping giant.	沉睡的巨人身旁有一只金盒子。
On the ground near the giant is a magic chest that appears to have been fashioned from ebony and rimmed on the edges with gold.	巨人附近的地上，擺著一只金盒子，看起來是用烏木打造，邊緣鑲著金邊。
The giant is carrying a chest.	巨人身上帶著一只金盒子。
There is a chest near the deceased giant.	已故巨人的身旁有一只金盒子。
The magic chest appears to have been fashioned from a solid block of maple and burnished to a brilliant luster.  The edges are rimmed with gold, as are the clasp and hinges.	這只金盒子似乎是用一整塊楓木打造，並且拋光得光亮動人。邊緣鑲著金邊，扣環與鉸鏈也都是金製的。
The giant is protecting the magic chest.	巨人正守護著這只金盒子。
The giant did a smashing job of defeating you.	巨人這一擊，把你打得粉身碎骨，乾淨俐落。
Slowly, carefully, you take the chest without waking the giant.	你小心翼翼、慢慢地拿走金盒子，沒有吵醒巨人。
